From 0a8112e5e31579ca7dd3a2a9b31573073efb88d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:10:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] film_lab: allow manual_range_contains, with the NaN
 reason

Clippy 1.97 flags nine `x < lo || x > hi` bounds tests across the
experiments (the 1.98.1 pin is not downloadable from this session, so the
gate ran on 1.97). The suggested `!(lo..=hi).contains(&x)` is not the same
function: it is true for NaN where the original is false, so it would
change which particles are culled. A crate-level allow with the reason,
rather than nine rewrites that alter behaviour.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nd3Ehrf9ktGu82K38kGEjH
---
 vieww_base/examples/film_lab/src/main.rs | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/vieww_base/examples/film_lab/src/main.rs b/vieww_base/examples/film_lab/src/main.rs
index 4592dff..2ffa3a3 100644
--- a/vieww_base/examples/film_lab/src/main.rs
+++ b/vieww_base/examples/film_lab/src/main.rs
@@ -136,6 +136,11 @@
 //! - `pidigits` — the counting axis: π banged out of two blocks
 //! - `pathtrace` — the light-transport axis: 1/√N, fitted; the furnace test
 
+// The experiments test bounds as `x < lo || x > hi`, which is false for NaN,
+// so a NaN value is never culled. `!(lo..=hi).contains(&x)` is true for NaN,
+// so the rewrite clippy suggests would change which particles are culled.
+#![allow(clippy::manual_range_contains)]
+
 mod exp_ant;
 mod exp_aurora;
 mod exp_avatar;
