From 072a4446496b6af0b2f3b50bae4de94073096c9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:10:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] vieww-paint: SSE2 compositing and output, the layer clear
 fused, x86-64-v2 restored
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PENDING §4.1. Byte-identical output throughout: all 30 gallery outputs
(stills, motion GIFs, interaction frames) compared against the pre-change
renderer, and each SIMD path held to its scalar reference bit for bit by
its own test (any NaN counts as one value; x86 picks which NaN by operand
order, which no output can observe — simd.rs's module doc).

- color::write_straight_u8: the RGBA8 output conversion, four pixels per
  16-byte store; true division, unfused multiplies, max/min/truncate as the
  saturating cast. Premul is now repr(C) so a pixel is one register.
- native/simd.rs: composite_flat's and composite_layer's normal-blend rows.
  The flat row keeps its two long-run branches; folding them into selects
  measured 10% worse on glass.
- Target::composite_layer_and_clear: zero each layer pixel as it is read,
  so the pool's clear has nothing to do. Timed rather than profiled
  (callgrind counts rep stosb per byte): nested 25.7 -> 22.0 ms median of
  ten interleaved runs. Falls back to composite + later clear whenever the
  read does not cover the whole ink box (a damage write mask) or the blend
  is not normal; a test covers both paths.
- .cargo/config.toml: -C target-cpu=x86-64-v2 for x86_64, which the file's
  reconstruction in 375aa13 had lost (floorf/ceilf were calls again).

callgrind, whole fixture run: 23-editor-glass 1,454M -> 1,172M,
00-layers-nested 1,573M -> 1,005M. Wall clock on a 2-core box: glass
~27 -> ~21 ms, nested ~28.5 -> ~20-22 ms, gallery 232.7 -> 164.6 ms. Both
still over 16.7 ms; PENDING §4.1 lists what is left. vieww-paint 272/272,
clippy clean on x86_64 and with the fallback cfg forced.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
