From 4cc66da6771a175caf6405a5c237a834a21996ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 09:43:10 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] GPU masks: upload only what changed; compact a churning
 atlas instead of growing it
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PENDING §2.1 asked to measure animated general paths before any MSAA work.
vieww-gpu's new examples/anim_paths does (120 frames, 1366x679): CPU
coverage is 0.37 ms a frame for a rotating star and ~1.3 ms for a rotating
600x360 panel — bounded, so no MSAA. The cost was the upload: any new mask
re-uploaded the whole mask texture, and the atlas, compacting only on live
texels, grew to 4096^2 under churn. 1.05 / 4.19 / 16.78 MB a frame for a
star / a panel / three moving shapes.

- MaskAtlas::changes_since(held): the rectangles blitted since the frame
  began, or Full after a compaction, a grow, or when the backend's copy is
  not the start-of-frame version (a skipped frame, a first upload).
- SceneRenderer::upload_masks: copies only those rectangles, transitioning
  from SHADER_READ_ONLY so the rest of the texture is kept; full upload
  otherwise. last_mask_upload_bytes() for tests and measurement.
- Compaction on the packing frontier (past 3/4) when at least half the
  packed texels are dead: a churning atlas compacts at its size, and the
  dead-half condition keeps it from compacting every frame.

Now 0.26 / 1.02 / 1.91 MB a frame on average. Tests: a model-texture replay
across compactions, grows and a skipped frame (mutation-checked: dropping
either full-rewrite mark fails it), and 48 animated frames on lavapipe each
byte-identical to a fresh renderer's full upload. GPU census parity
unchanged. vieww-gpu 71/71; vieww-hal vulkan 45/46, the one failure being
the known PENDING §2.2 backdrop-blur edge, identical before this change.

Also: vulkan_compute's workgroup-reduction test overflowed in its own input
generator (Knuth's hash with a plain `*`; debug builds panic) — now
wrapping_mul. It failed identically before this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Nd3Ehrf9ktGu82K38kGEjH
