MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

PENDING §1.7's next increment. GpuRenderer now chooses per frame: the
unlit pass for Basic-only scenes, a new lit pass when any material is
Lambert. Both held to the CPU oracle in interiors on lavapipe.

- vieww-shaders: lit3d.wgsl — the CPU's `shade` for Basic and Lambert,
  term for term and in light order: ambient, hemisphere, directional;
  the CPU's ShadowMap::visibility (orthographic light VP, truncated texel
  coordinates, 3x3 PCF, slope-scaled bias); the same sRGB encode.
- vieww-hal: render_unlit3d_to_pixels refactored into a shared one-shot
  render_3d_pass (interleaved vertices, uniform at binding 0, optional
  fragment storage buffer at binding 1); the unlit entry point is a thin
  wrapper (its parity tests unchanged and green), render_lit3d_to_pixels
  the second.
- vieww-3d: render.rs shares world_lights, Item, ShadowMap and
  shadow_pass with gpu.rs, so the GPU path sums the same lights in the
  same order and uploads the CPU's own shadow map. gpu.rs collects the
  visible items once, packs de-indexed vertices for the lit pass, and
  decides back faces per triangle (cull single-sided, flip double-sided)
  by the side of the plane the eye is on — equivalent to the CPU's
  screen-area sign for geometry in front of the camera.
- Falls back to the CPU for the whole frame on: point/spot lights, IBL
  or GI, more than 8 lights, any other shading, textures, transparency.

tests/gpu_lit.rs (4, lavapipe): lit scene (smooth + flat Lambert,
rotated box, coloured second light, a Basic box in the same draw), a
long cast shadow, single- and double-sided back faces, and a point-light
scene falling back to the CPU exactly. Mutation-checked: no shadow lookup
-> 1,644 interior mismatches; no back-face flip -> 4,670. vieww-3d 86/86
with vulkan (77/77 without), vieww-shaders 24/24, clippy clean.

